        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Middle East war escalates after attack on key Iranian gas field Middle East Issued on: 19/03/2026 - 16:34 Modified: 19/03/2026 - 16:42 #Israel hit Iranian's part of the South Pars #gas field, the world's largest offshore reservoir #Tehran shares with #Doha, on March 18. In retaliation for the strikes, #Iran ramped up its attacks on Gulf countries' energy infrastructures, sending #oil prices soaring. Israel also reported strikes on its refineries on March 19. Steven Everts: For Europeans, war on Iran 'a diversion' and 'giant gift to Putin' 19/03/2026 Middle East Iran: Saudi Arabia warns of 'military action' over repeated attacks 19/03/2026 Middle East Ayman Mhanna: 'Lebanon has become the theatre for a war between Israel and Iran' 19/03/2026 Middle East Qatar orders departure of two Iranian diplomats over gas facility attack 18/03/2026 Middle East 'Acute risk' that Iraq could become once again victim of internal conflict as Iran war progresses 18/03/2026 Middle East Iran did not try to rebuild enrichment after June 2025 attack, US intel chief says 18/03/2026 Middle East Both sides in Iran war ratchet up attacks on energy facilities, as oil prices surge 18/03/2026 Middle East Elisa Catalano Ewers: Israeli leadership moves to destabilise regime’s leadership structure 18/03/2026 Middle East Soler i Lecha: Foreign policy of Pedro Sánchez 'widely supported by the Spanish population' 18/03/2026 Spain"
