        "orario": "16:20",
        "timestamp": 1773933618,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Steven Everts: For Europeans, war on Iran 'a diversion' and 'giant gift to Putin' Middle East Issued on: 19/03/2026 - 16:20 Modified: 19/03/2026 - 16:26 Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Steven Everts, Director of European Union Institute for Security Studies (EUISS). According to Mr. Everts, the current conflict is an unnecessary war defined by cycles of retaliation that risk expanding beyond their original scope, with serious implications for regional stability and global energy markets. Europe is already feeling the economic fallout, but the deeper concern lies in the possibility of further destabilisation. He sees this war as strategically counterproductive, not only for Europe but for broader international stability. Iran: Saudi Arabia warns of 'military action' over repeated attacks 19/03/2026 Middle East Ayman Mhanna: 'Lebanon has become the theatre for a war between Israel and Iran' 19/03/2026 Middle East Qatar orders departure of two Iranian diplomats over gas facility attack 18/03/2026 Middle East 'Acute risk' that Iraq could become once again victim of internal conflict as Iran war progresses 18/03/2026 Middle East Iran did not try to rebuild enrichment after June 2025 attack, US intel chief says 18/03/2026 Middle East Both sides in Iran war ratchet up attacks on energy facilities, as oil prices surge 18/03/2026 Middle East Elisa Catalano Ewers: Israeli leadership moves to destabilise regime’s leadership structure 18/03/2026 Middle East Soler i Lecha: Foreign policy of Pedro Sánchez 'widely supported by the Spanish population' 18/03/2026 Spain Crowds gather for funeral of top security official Ali Larijani 18/03/2026 Middle East"
